==Trivia==
*The Firecracker's weapon resembles [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoulder-fired_missile man-portable rocket launchers]. Rocket Launchers were first developed in ancient China in the ninth century. Originally, they were firing multiple arrows together in a device called [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_arrow fire arrow], until they were replaced with rocket motors during the twelfth century.
**In the Turkish and Portuguese language settings of the game, the Firecracker's name translates to "Pyrotechnist". In the Dutch and Indonesian language settings of the game, the Firecracker's name translates to "Fireworks Shooter". In the French, Spanish, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Russian, Arabic, Chinese, Malaysian, Thai, and Finnish language settings of the game, the Firecracker's name translates to "Artificer", "Firethrower", "Pyrotechnic Archer", "Rocket Gunner", "Rocketeer", "Fire Archer", "Fireworks Thrower", "Fireworks Gunner", "Firecracker Shooter", "Firework Archer", and "Firewoman" respectively.
**According to a [https://x.com/Seth_Supercell/status/1212713267543576577?s=20 tweet], the Firecracker's firework is taken from an Air Defense from Clash of Clans.
*The Firecracker's Evolution was one of the first [[Card Evolution|Evolutions]] to be added in the game, alongside the [[Skeletons/Evolution|Skeletons]], [[Barbarians/Evolution|Barbarians]], and [[Royal Giant/Evolution|Royal Giant]]. It is also one of the first evolved [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] to be featured in a [[Loading Screens|Loading Screen]], alongside the Barbarians, Royal Giant, and Skeletons.
*The Firecracker's Evolution is 1 of 5 evolved troops which can defeat themselves in one attack, the others being [[Skeletons/Evolution|Skeletons]], [[Wall Breakers/Evolution|Wall Breakers]], Runners, and [[Goblin Barrel/Evolution|Decoy Goblins]].
*From her description, it is implied that the Firecracker is [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyromania pyromaniac].
*The spread angle between the leftmost and rightmost small projectiles is 70 degrees, which means the angle between any two adjacent small projectiles is 17.5 degrees.
*The Firecracker's Evolution is the subject of an [[Emotes|Emote]].
*The initial balance change for Evolved Firecracker on the [[Version History#Balance Changes (8/8/2023)|8/8/2023 balance changes]] was a hitpoints decrease to 133% of the original's and a decrease to the Big and Small Spark's duration to 2 seconds (from 2.5 seconds) and 1.5 seconds (from 2 seconds), but the hitpoints decrease was raised to 130% and the Big and Small Spark's duration decreases were [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-50-balance-wip pulled back last minute].

